      "title": "aibleton-skeleton-setup",
      "firstPrompt": "I would like to make a new application that acts as a bandmate while practicing or playing an instrument. Initially, we will focus on bandmates for drummers. The main idea is that there is a service that runs on a user's machine, called 'mate'. This service will provide an api, connect to the mcp servers, and to the anthropic api. There will also be a nextjs app (use create-next-app), called 'app', that can hit that api and provide some state information. It will provide a very stripped down DAW-type view (multiple tracks and what is on them -- no realtime playback). Everything will be written in typescript, and mate will run on bun. Mate should have a specific, testable, stubbable intelligence module. This module will run a simple agent loop (yet to be defined, but a state machine). This loop will not be expected to operate in realtime, but will have a mailbox that it checks periodically for new commands. These commands could be generated by the loop itself or from hardware (perhaps I add a midi controller later), timing, api calls, etc. It will have a good abstraction for ableton so that we can operate the stack without it if we want, and have the intelligence and API still running. It will also have a good abstraction for splice, with dummy data, that helps demonstrate functionality if splice is missing. Make a plan for creating the skeleton of this application, i.e. folder structure, main modules stubbed, abstractions stubbed, etc.",
